<h2 id="settings">Request settings</h2>
<p>All variants are fresh runs on the unchanged panel. The context budget includes the entire prompt,
reasoning and answer. For each question, the requested output allowance is
<code>min(endpoint output limit, 262144 − exact prompt tokens)</code>. Prompts are never shortened.
For hosted models whose server context is larger, the comparison client enforces this total budget through
the output allowance; it does not reconfigure the provider's model architecture.</p>
<p>No fixed seed is requested for any model. Hosted models request high reasoning effort;
Nemotron's provider mapping and capacity investigation are described below. Local models have
thinking enabled. The controls are model-specific and do not establish equal reasoning compute. Frequency
and presence penalties are zero, and repetition penalty is one for adjustable models. Local min-p filtering
is explicitly disabled. Top-k disabled is encoded as <code>0</code> by OpenRouter and <code>-1</code> by vLLM.
Natural model termination tokens remain model-specific; no benchmark answer string is used to stop generation.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Variant</th><th>Temperature</th><th>Top-p</th><th>Top-k</th>
<th>Reasoning request</th><th>Provider route</th><th>Total budget</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for name, model in models.items() %}<tr><th>{{ name }}</th>
{% if model.get('sampling_exception') %}<td>Fixed provider sampling</td><td>Unsupported</td><td>Unsupported</td>
{% else %}<td>{{ model.extra.temperature }}</td><td>{{ model.extra.top_p }}</td><td>Disabled ({{ model.extra.top_k }})</td>{% endif %}
<td>{{ 'Full output allowance minus one token' if model.get('reasoning_budget_policy') else model.extra.get('reasoning_effort', 'Thinking enabled') }}</td>
<td>{{ model.extra.provider.only[0] if model.extra.get('provider') else 'Marin vLLM' if name in ['standardized-mochi', 'standardized-snowball', 'standardized-grug-datakit'] else 'vLLM' }}</td>
<td>262,144</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>
<p>OpenRouter routes require the declared parameters and disable provider fallbacks. Parameter-acceptance
probes succeeded for Kimi, DeepSeek, GLM and Nemotron. Kimi moves from Moonshot to Fireworks to expose top-k;
this provider change is part of its recorded condition. GLM uses Fireworks, because its earlier direct endpoint
is unavailable. Nemotron is <code>nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b</code> through DeepInfra's BF16 priority route.
Provider labels do not establish an independently verified weight revision or quantization.</p>
{% if nemotron_comparison %}
<p>Nemotron's initial high-effort run returned {{ nemotron_comparison.uncapped_results }} usable responses
and {{ nemotron_comparison.provider_clamps }} responses cut off at 65,536 output tokens despite larger
requested allowances. These are provider clamps, not demonstrated native context limits. The replacement
is a fresh run on all 88 questions, with <code>reasoning.max_tokens = max_tokens − 1</code> instead of
<code>reasoning_effort</code>; both fields cannot be supplied together. The total output allowance, sampling
and route are unchanged. This is a model-specific reasoning control, not equal reasoning compute.
Earlier answers and capacity probes are excluded from its headline; their budget comparison is preserved
in the evidence. Requests are still checked for provider clamps before scoring.</p>
{% else %}
<p>Nemotron remains provisional. Six initial responses stopped at 65,536 tokens despite larger requested
allowances. November 17 upstream-debug probes showed that OpenRouter maps its requested high reasoning
effort to DeepInfra medium effort. Explicit reasoning budgets and the output-budget alias did not avoid
that mapping; a longer explicit-budget probe reproduced the 65K cutoff. The candidate replacement was held
before launch. These are unresolved provider limits, not demonstrated native context limits of the weights.
They are kept separate from completed model answers.</p>
{% endif %}
<p>The Astra and Opus exceptions were chosen before collection after rejected temperature-0.7 probes.
Their limitations are documented by <a href="https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/changelog">OpenAI</a>
and <a href="https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/thinking">Anthropic</a>.</p>

<h2 id="results">Accuracy</h2>
<p>The headline gives each family equal weight; question accuracy gives each question equal weight.
Truncated and malformed returned answers are incorrect. Missing responses remain missing and produce
lower–upper bounds, not confidence intervals. Native output-limit truncations and full-context exhaustion
are counted separately. Provider clamps and interrupted streams remain collection failures. Truncation and
format-error counts can overlap.</p>
