<h2>Model identities and token allowances</h2>
<p>Snowball uses the pinned v0.1.1 release at its native 256K context; Qwen also uses its native 256K
configuration. Mochi uses Hero SFT step 400407 in BF16, with the same weights, tokenizer route and thinking
adapter as the original Mochi run. It is evaluated afresh for this condition. Reasoning delimiters are preserved
in the raw response and only the final answer is scored; unfinished reasoning cannot supply an answer.</p>
{% if models.get('standardized-grug-datakit') %}
<p><code>standardized-grug-datakit</code> uses
<a href="https://huggingface.co/open-athena/Grug-67B-A2B-Datakit-SFT-262K-2026.10.05/blob/ac60d9401820953943f5a56e06f36e13c86b12d6/README.md">Grug-67B-A2B-Datakit-SFT-262K-2026.10.05</a>,
pinned to revision <code>ac60d9401820953943f5a56e06f36e13c86b12d6</code>, in BF16.
This is a separate checkpoint from Snowball. Its card declares 262,144 tokens but states that
long-context generation has not been validated.
{% if context_preflight.get('standardized-grug-datakit') %}
The benchmark verified checkpoint hashes, the live 262,144-token registry and exact tokenisation
of all 88 prompts; these checks establish admission, not long-context accuracy.
{% else %}
Serving jobs are queued for GPU capacity. Live server verification and all-prompt tokenisation
must pass before evaluation; no Grug accuracy is available yet.
{% endif %}
Thinking is enabled, both native end tokens (128001 and 128009) are retained,
and the same <code>marin-thinking-v1</code> answer adapter used for Mochi excludes unfinished reasoning.
Full responses, including special tokens, are available in the
<a href="../questions/?model=standardized-grug-datakit">question browser</a>.</p>
{% endif %}
