<h2>Evaluation and provenance</h2>
<p>One response per model and question is selected. Completed answers are not retried based on score.
Transport failures retain their partial streams and can receive a separately recorded retry with the same
parameters and full allowance. The runner never executes tools. Requests explicitly disable tools and the
OpenRouter web plugin, and raw responses are audited for tool events. Every published answer is bound to
its frozen prompt, request controls, token budget and response hash, then rescored under the unchanged contract.</p>
<p>MECH and the separate F01/F02 sequence-prediction tracks are excluded. These are descriptive scores for
a previously exposed 88-question panel; questions sharing source structures are not independent proteins.
The <a href="../questions/">question browser</a> publishes exact prompts, oracle answers and full model
message fields, including available reasoning and preserved partial text from terminal collection failures.
The public evidence also contains per-question token counts, request controls, hashes and collection-failure categories.</p>
